        "original_id": "3f483795-bc47-53d2-8951-bf8fed38f0a1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Langtry, Texas; Val Verde County, Texas\n- People: Roy Bean\n- Roles: saloon-keeper; Justice of the Peace\n- Concepts: \"The Law West of the Pecos\"\n\nFacts:\n- Phantly Roy Bean, Jr. was born around 1825 and died on March 16, 1903.\n- Roy Bean was an eccentric U.S. saloon-keeper and Justice of the Peace in Val Verde County, Texas.\n- Roy Bean called himself \"The Law West of the Pecos.\"\n- Langtry, Texas, is notable as the place where Roy Bean had his saloon and practiced law.\n- Roy Bean was also known as Judge Roy Bean.",
